-- title:
--   Residual ordinarity at p of a Hecke–Galois datum
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$ and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta \neq 0$ which is a semistable model, i.e. no prime $q$ with $q \mid \Delta$ satisfies $q \mid c_4$. Assume the $p$-torsion of $W_{\mathbb{Q}}$ over an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ has exactly $p^2$ elements and that the resulting action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ on it is trivial on the automorphisms fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; write $\bar\rho_W$ for the associated rank-two representation over $\mathbb{Z}/p$. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes with $p \in S$ containing every prime dividing $\Delta$. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring, complete for its maximal ideal, with finite residue field and $p$ in the maximal ideal, and $\iota : \mathbb{Z}/p \to \mathcal{O}/\mathfrak{m}$ a ring homomorphism such that the base change of $\bar\rho_W$ along $\iota$ stays irreducible over an algebraic closure of $\mathcal{O}/\mathfrak{m}$. Let $N \neq 0$ be such that every prime dividing $N$ lies in $S$, that $q^2 \mid N$ for $q \in S$ with $q \neq p$, that $p \mid N$ and $p^2 \nmid N$ whenever $p \mid \Delta$ or $p \nmid a_p(W)$, and that $p \nmid N$ whenever $p \nmid \Delta$ and $p \mid a_p(W)$, where $a_\ell(W) = \ell + 1 - \#(W \bmod \ell)$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two Hecke algebra of level $N$ generated by the operators outside $S$ to $\mathcal{O}/\mathfrak{m}$ with $\theta(T_\ell)$ the residue of $a_\ell(W)$ for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ outside $S$, let $T$ be a complete noetherian local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module with local structure map, and let $H$ be a Hecke–Galois datum for these data: a lift $\pi$ of $\theta$ to $T$ whose image generates $T$ over $\mathcal{O}$, with the stated point-lifting and residual surjectivity properties, together with a rank-two $T$-adic Galois representation $\rho$ whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at primes $\ell \nmid N$ outside $S$ are $X^2 - \pi(T_\ell)X + \ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible. Assume $p \mid \Delta$ or $p \nmid a_p(W)$. Then the residual representation of $H.\rho$, read as a Galois representation over the field $T/\mathfrak{m}_T$, is ordinary at $p$: for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $p$ is a nonunit there is a submodule $L$ of the representation space which is spanned by the first member of some basis indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\ 2$, is stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and contains $\rho(\sigma)v - v$ for every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup and every $v$.
--
--   This is the curve-side input to the ordinary deformation condition: it transfers ordinarity at $p$ of the mod-$p$ representation of a semistable elliptic curve that is multiplicative or ordinary at $p$ to the residual representation attached to a weight-two Hecke–Galois datum congruent to it. It feeds the dichotomy [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.ordinaryCondition_or_flatCondition_of_apOfModel`](thm.html#CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.ordinaryCondition_or_flatCondition_of_apOfModel), which selects the ordinary or the flat local condition according to the behaviour of $W$ at $p$.
